    "body": "> I was going to nominate WebApps given it maintains the Gamepad API, which is both similar as a peripheral API and has overlap in the engineers working as editors and implementers.\n\nI can live with that (though for the same reasons as DAS, WebApps has too many specs :( ). \n\n> Based on my assessment, a new WG would be too costly and is unlikely to garner support from the W3C membership.\n\nRight, but that needs to be balanced against DAS **and** WebApps have too many specs already, which also means that both groups are too costly to join. \n\nThis is a larger problem that we need to address by creating a new group at some point.  \n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
