    "created_at": "2026-01-15T16:19:05Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-15T16:19:05Z",
    "body": "If appropriately related in scope, I don't see the concern of adding into\r\nthe Web apps working group. Yes, there are several specifications there,\r\nbut I'm not sure how putting them in another working group would improve\r\nthe overall progress in the portfolio. If anything it would cause\r\nscheduling conflicts at things like tpac.\r\n\r\nI think the joint approach is quite good, given the scopes of the groups.\r\nThis should also minimize any companies need when considering participating\r\nas most companies expected to participate in these have already engaged in\r\nthese working groups, and it seems the incremental evaluation of charter\r\nupdates is easier than joining new groups.\r\n\r\nOn Thu, Jan 15, 2026, 2:32 AM Anssi Kostiainen ***@***.***>\r\nwrote:\r\n\r\n> *anssiko* left a comment (WICG/serial#218)\r\n> <https://github.com/WICG/serial/issues/218#issuecomment-3754071956>\r\n>\r\n> Mozilla has participated the DAS WG and has implemented and shipped APIs\r\n> produced by the group in its now discontinued FirefoxOS product and certain\r\n> versions of its Firefox browser. Re-joining WGs is normal and happens from\r\n> time to time when companies' priorities change. I welcome Mozilla back to\r\n> the DAS WG.\r\n>\r\n> We have initiated charter refinement process to seek W3C community\r\n> consensus on this important matter.\r\n>\r\n> —\r\n> Reply to this email directly, view it on GitHub\r\n> <https://github.com/WICG/serial/issues/218#issuecomment-3754071956>, or\r\n> unsubscribe\r\n> <https://github.com/notifications/unsubscribe-auth/AAC6PG2HB4D2VJHJXLPDVWT4G5UCXAVCNFSM6AAAAACRSUWTJ6VHI2DSMVQWIX3LMV43OSLTON2WKQ3PNVWWK3TUHMZTONJUGA3TCOJVGY>\r\n> .\r\n> You are receiving this because you are subscribed to this thread.Message\r\n> ID: ***@***.***>\r\n>\r\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
