    "created_at": "2026-03-11T15:26:24Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-03-11T15:26:24Z",
    "body": "> What would be cool is if we had some kind of working group that allowed us to do APIs that have a security model that goes beyond the Web's current one: like, Mozilla is not going to expose this API to every website, IIUC. They are only exposing it on a _per requested site basis_ through their web extensions mechanism. Grouping APIs like that somehow (and into a new working group) seems like potentially a good idea (to me).\n\nJust to clarify: Mozilla is going to expose this API to every website. The first time a website attempts to use the API, the browser will generate a web extension and request permission to install it. (the web extension itself doesn't really do anything; the point is to make it clear to the user that this is an unusual and dangerous permission that the website is requesting) This is the same model we are using for WebMIDI.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
